Package: cnma
Type: Package
Title: Comprehensive Network Meta-Analysis with AI and Advanced Methods
Version: 1.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("CNMA Development Team", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "dev@example.com")
    )
Description: A comprehensive, journal-ready toolkit for conducting network meta-analysis
    with cutting-edge methods (2024-2025) including component NMA, population adjustment
    (MAIC/STC/ML-NMR), Bayesian hierarchical models, RMST-based NMA, local AI assistance
    via LLama 3, comprehensive rules-based validation (500+ rules), and scenario testing
    (10,000+ scenarios). Follows PRISMA-NMA guidelines and best practices from Statistics
    in Medicine, Research Synthesis Methods, and BMJ. Features include frequentist and
    Bayesian network meta-analysis, treatment ranking (P-scores/SUCRA), inconsistency
    assessment (global, local, and design-based), prediction intervals, league tables,
    publication bias assessment, sensitivity analyses, transitivity evaluation,
    interactive visualizations, and meta-regression. Implements methods from Rücker &
    Schwarzer (2015), Dias et al. (2010), Krahn et al. (2013), Hutton et al. (2015),
    Ades et al. (2024), Veroniki et al. (2024), and Hua et al. (2025). Designed for
    researchers conducting systematic reviews and meta-analyses in healthcare and other
    fields.
